<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="messages_filter_help.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="messages_filter_help">
    <!-- Message-log filter-help overlay (Messages::dialog, FILTER action). A
         passive backdrop stacked UNDER the curses string_input "filter" line,
         replacing the curses w_filter_help box — the same role autopickup_help /
         safemode_help play for their string_input popups. The syntax help is
         DYNAMIC (it lists the registered message-type names, coloured by type),
         so unlike those static helps it is data-bound (help_rml) rather than
         literal in the .rml. The bottom row is left blank for the curses input
         field, which composites on top. -->
    <div class="mfh-wrap">
        <div class="panel mfh-panel">
            <div class="mfh-text" data-rml="help_rml"></div>
            <div class="mfh-input-row"></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
